#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0152 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#note "Positive control AND a second pin on the same defect. Only row 1 is defective (ABLFL=Y with BASE 1.5 not equal to AVAL 2.5); row 2 is a conformant baseline record and row 3 is guarded out by ABLFL=N. Before the value_is_reference fix this fixture yielded 2 violations rather than 1, because the leaf fired on every record passing the ABLFL/non_empty guards irrespective of whether BASE equalled AVAL - row 2 reported as well. It yields exactly 1 after the fix."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ABLFL   type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col BASE    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | Y | 2.5 | 1.5
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALT | Y | 7.0 | 7.0
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALT | N | 9.9 | 7.0
---
